The '''Anhangá Liberation Movement''' ({{lang-bl|Movimento de Liberación Anhangá}}, '''MLA'''; {{Lang-ku|''Anhangá Etêng Mbya'ai Vy'a''}}) is a [[Balisca]]n {{W|political organization|political}} and militant organization founded on 27 April 1920. At its height in 1950, the MLA numbered about 100,000 members and associates. The group emerged from various {{W|indigenismo|indigenist}} organizations, mainly in [[Cerdanya]], establishing their base of support among the rural Indigenous communities across the community. 

The MLA was created with the goal of the dissolution of the Baliscan state and other Latin American countries, which they consider to be illegitimate remnants of European [[W:Imperialism|imperialism]] and {{W|settler colonialism}}. 
